## be checked headless (tests/test_last_shift_rooms.gd). GENERATED by tools/gen_rooms.py: edit
## the generator and run it again (python tools/gen_rooms.py), not this file.
##
## Map legend:  #  wall     .  floor     A  wall with the employer's logo sign (background dressing)
##              H  hedge (outdoors; solid like a wall)
## Door cells in the wall line are '.' in the map; the door prop covers them.
## Props use tile rects: Rect2i(x, y, w, h). Spawns are tile cells plus the way Nash faces.
## "when" on a prop/enemy/person: "calm" (before the alarms), "alarm" (after they start),
## "after_attack" (after the Day 0 scene in the plant).
## "diff" on an enemy: 0 = always, 1 = Normal and Hard only, 2 = Hard only.
## "loot" on a prop: it can be searched (2 s); [{"item", "n"}...], [] = nothing inside.
## "note" on a container: an email/note id shown after searching it.
## "npcs": ambient people (last_shift_npc.gd); "bark" is a key of LsText.BARKS.
##
## Main route: parking lot (dusk) -> lobby -> elevator -> plant -> corridor -> pump room -> locker
## room -> break room -> security hall -> security office -> open office -> call center -> lobby hall
## -> lobby (barricade) -> parking lot (dawn).
## Other ways out: break room -> cafeteria -> loading dock (Dwayne's key) -> service yard;
## open office -> server floor -> fire exit (bolt cutters from the cooling floor) -> side street.
## Dead ends: cooling floor, armory, server room, customer service offices, janitor's closet.

